it; weekly closes under $423.52 mean it is stalling below your 2.618.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"what-would-change-this-read\">What would change this read</h3>\n<ul><li>The Nov 16 settlement hearing: approval eases the worry, rejection reopens it.</li><li>Fiscal Q1 results (date not found): watch incentive growth against revenue growth, and US volume against the +10% of October.</li><li>A weekly close under $392.38, or a weekly close over $442.75.</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"confidence-and-sources\">Confidence and sources</h3>\n<p>Results are solid. The outlook and quote were read twice, from an automated transcript; Visa's own release page would not load, so a full copy was used. The 28.5% incentive share is my arithmetic from 10-K lines, not Visa's figure. Legal status comes from the 10-K and trade press. Share prices are Webull daily bars, adjusted for dividends, so they differ slightly from your thinkorswim readings.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.jamessharp.co.uk/market-news/visa-q4-full-year-results-2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release copy</a> · <a href=\"https://www.webull.com/news/15822495508279296\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Call transcript</a> · <a href=\"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3017664/visa-q4-earnings-call-highlights-fy27-outlook-and-growth-priorities\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Call recap</a> · <a href=\"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3017346/visa-q4-earnings-beat-estimates-on-strong-payment-volumes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Results recap</a> · <a href=\"https://www.americanbanker.com/payments/news/visa-says-you-can-thank-the-labor-market-for-strong-spending\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">American Banker</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001403161/000140316126000134/v-20260930.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">10-K</a> · <a href=\"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1403161/000130817925000630/v-20251126.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Proxy</a> · <a href=\"https://s1.q4